# TCP-fragmentation replay: a single 32-byte '$' record is split across three 'hex:' lines, exactly
# as consecutive stream reads might deliver it. extractFrames() must hold the partial buffer and
# emit the frame only once the final bytes arrive. Frames are always built through extractFrames(),
# so this fixture fails if the reassembly logic ever regresses.

# An ASCII packet first, so the trailing X-mode record has a device ID to inherit.
*TH,2020916012,V1,050316,A,2212.8745,N,11346.6574,E,14.28,028,220902,FFFFFBFF#
# The same '$' record, delivered in three fragments -> recorded.
hex:242020916012050316
hex:2209022212874500
hex:113466574E014028FFFFFBFFFF0001
# X-mode record with no ID of its own -> inherits 2020916012, recorded.
hex:5820209160120503162209022212874500113466574E014028FFFFFBFFFF0001
